Subject: [PATCH] kernel: add LaunchTrace startup read recorder hooks
Target: Linux 4.4 commit afd2ff9b7e1b367172f18ba7f693dfb62bdcb2dc

The module cannot be called directly from built-in kernel objects. Add the
small built-in dispatch layer in kernel/launchtrace.c; the loadable recorder
registers callbacks and pins its module while a callback is running.

1. Copy launchtrace.h to include/linux/launchtrace.h.
2. Copy launchtrace-core.c to kernel/launchtrace.c.
3. Add `obj-y += launchtrace.o` to kernel/Makefile.
4. Add the hook calls below.
5. Build/load the external module from this directory.

--- a/fs/exec.c
+++ b/fs/exec.c
@@
 #include <linux/compat.h>
+#include <linux/launchtrace.h>
@@
 	if (IS_ERR(filename))
 		return PTR_ERR(filename);
+	/* Experimental: starts capture before exec success is known. */
+	launchtrace_exec_start(filename->name);

--- a/block/blk-core.c
+++ b/block/blk-core.c
@@
 #include <linux/fault-inject.h>
+#include <linux/launchtrace.h>
@@
 blk_qc_t submit_bio(int rw, struct bio *bio)
 {
 	bio->bi_rw |= rw;
+	/* Observe read BIOs before generic_make_request can remap/split them. */
+	if (!(rw & WRITE))
+		launchtrace_bio_submit(bio);

--- a/kernel/exit.c
+++ b/kernel/exit.c
@@
 #include <linux/oom.h>
+#include <linux/launchtrace.h>
@@
 	group_dead = atomic_dec_and_test(&tsk->signal->live);
+	/* One notification for the last exiting thread in this thread group. */
+	if (group_dead)
+		launchtrace_task_exit(task_tgid_nr(tsk));

IMPORTANT: The exit hunk is a placement guide. Verify the exact local context
and variable names in the complete target checkout. The callback must run
only on the group_dead path, not once for every thread. The exec hook is
intentionally before successful exec completion; failed-exec rollback is
not implemented in this version.
